<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Jeddah (1927)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1927</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Jeddah, signed on 20 May 1927 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a>, recognised the full independence of his Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a> and its dependencies, replacing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-darin">Treaty of Darin</a> of 1915, which had made Nejd a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. Ibn Saud in turn recognised Britain's special treaty relations with the Gulf sheikhdoms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jeddah-1927.jpg" alt="Treaty of Jeddah (1927)" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UK Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_Foreign_office_memorandum_January_1940_regarding_the_border_between_Jordan_and_Saudi_Arabia.djvu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
